  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[cms-for-your-fridge]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[A CMS for Your Fridge]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Publish the leftovers. Unpublish the milk.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Publish Leftovers
Milk Rollback
Shelf Tree
Expiry Alert]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Content strategy for shelf two | A governance model for the middle shelf. Workshops are planned. The cheese has not replied.
Go headless | Decouple the food from the door. API-first leftovers. Cold air on every channel.
Migrate from the old fridge | Lift and shift 400 items. Half are from 2019. 'We'll clean up after go-live.'
Single source of truth for milk | One system that knows whether there is milk. It is not Dad. Dad always says 'plenty'.
Omnichannel leftovers | The same lasagne in fridge, freezer and lunchbox. Create once, reheat everywhere.
Upgrade the fridge to latest major | From v7 to v17 in one go. Estimate: a weekend. Actual: we don't talk about it.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Scheduled unpublish | As a yoghurt, I want an unpublish date so that I am not live in prod three weeks past it.
Approval workflow | As a flatmate, I want two-step approval on my leftovers so that 'I thought it was shared' is logged.
Rollback | As a user, I want to roll back to the version with cake in it so that I can undo last night.
Preview mode | As a hungry user, I want a preview so that I stop standing with the door open like a stuck build.
Admin role for Mum | As a mum, I want to be the only admin so that the mustard stays where the content model says.
Stay in draft | As Tuesday's leftovers, I want to stay in draft so that nobody publishes me to a lunchbox.
Find the lost jar | As a jar of pickles from 2019, I want to show up in search so that somebody finally remembers me.
Staging shelf | As a carton of milk, I want a staging shelf so that I am tested before I reach anybody's coffee.
Content freeze | As a project manager, I want a content freeze before Christmas so that the freezer has a purpose.
Lunch access control | As a colleague, I want my lunch access-controlled so that 'NAME ON IT!!' can finally retire.
The client wants a carousel | As a client, I want a carousel on the top shelf so that the important cheese rotates past nobody.
Reject the hot pot | As a fridge, I want hot pots submitted as pull requests so that I can reject them properly.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Document type: Leftover | Properties: what, when, and a mandatory 'do we dare?' checkbox.
Media library: magnets | All your magnets, three pizza menus and one drawing from 2016, in folders.
404 Milk Not Found | A custom error page with directions to the nearest corner shop.
Recycle bin | 30 days retention. On a fridge this is known as the vegetable drawer.
Cold cache | It is all cache. It is a fridge. Clear it by leaving the door open.
Publish with descendants | Publish the Christmas duck and everything under it. Gravy included.
Rich text editor for notes | Bold, italic and passive-aggressive. 'To whoever took my yoghurt.'
Version history: mustard | See who had it, when, and how little they left.
Scheduled publish: defrosting | Moves the meat from freezer to fridge 24 hours before go-live.
Door login with 2FA | A code and a reason. 'Just looking' is not a reason.
Block grid for shelves | Drag-and-drop shelves in 12 columns. The cucumber spans all of them.
Broken link checker | Finds the half lemon that no recipe links to anymore.
Content template: meal plan | Monday to Friday prefilled. Friday always resolves to pizza.
Health check dashboard | Green: milk. Yellow: the cheese. Red: do not open the blue box.
Multi-site: the freezer | Same backoffice, second site. Nobody has edited it since launch.
Dictionary item: 'best before' | Translates 'best before' to 'still fine, probably' on every label.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Light is on when the door is closed | Cannot reproduce. Cannot observe. Three seniors have left philosophical comments.
Milk published without content | Empty carton put back on the shelf. Author unknown. Everyone suspects the same node.
Butter node was moved | Butter is no longer under /door/top. All links broken. Morning routine is down.
Lunch visible to all members | Permissions on 'Colleague's lunch' set to Everyone. Incident at 11:58. Again at 12:03.
Duplicate content: 4 open ketchups | Editors keep creating new instead of searching. Search works. Users don't.
Fridge hums when Umbraco restarts | Probably unrelated. Happens on every app pool recycle. Reopened.
Expiry date in US format | 03/04 was read as April. It was March. The reporter has been home for two days.
Unpublished cheese still cached | Removed on Tuesday, still detectable on Friday. Cleared the cache. It is in the walls.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[Nobody has the backoffice password | Whoever set up the fridge moved out in 2021. We go in through the freezer.
The jar at the back | Legacy content. No owner, no label, load-bearing. Remove it and the shelf comes down.
Temperature is hardcoded to 'ish' | The dial goes from 1 to 7. Nobody knows which end is cold. It stays on 4 'to be safe'.
Custom property editor for eggs | Built by a freelancer in 2018. Holds exactly six. We buy ten. The rest live in the door.
400 unused document types | 'Test', 'Test2', 'Mustard_NEW', 'DO NOT USE'. All in use. Especially DO NOT USE.
The freezer still runs v7 | The upgrade is in the backlog under 'Q3'. Nobody has ever said which Q3.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[Otto Request: Can the fridge do AI? | 'It should know what I want before I open it.' It is always the last slice of cake.
Otto Request: Fridge on the homepage | 'A live feed of the office fridge, right in the hero. People love authenticity.'
Otto Request: Why can't I just edit it? | 'In Word I just type.' Said with the door open for four full minutes.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Publish your leftovers with confidence.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[The first headless CMS for your fridge. Schedule the milk, version the mustard, and unpublish that jar from 2019 before it unpublishes you.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Log in to your fridge]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Editor-friendly | Mum can move the butter without calling a developer. She will call anyway. We have built a queue.
Scheduled unpublish | Every yoghurt gets an expiry workflow. No more content that has been live since before the summer holidays.
Truly headless | We removed the door. Your food is now available on every channel, including the floor.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[We migrated 400 items from the old fridge. Three are still in 'Mustard_NEW'. Nobody dares touch them.
I rolled back to the version with cake in it. Game changer.
It says 404 Milk Not Found. It is right. It is always right.
The upgrade would take a weekend, they said. That was in March. The freezer is still on v7.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free up to three shelves. Enterprise (freezer plus vegetable drawer): call for a quote. We will estimate it wrong.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© A CMS for Your Fridge. Best before: see lid. Cookies? Bottom shelf, behind the pickles.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
